```lean
theorem minWeight_le (G : FiniteHeatOperator X) (h : ∃ x y : X, x ≠ y) {x y : X} (hxy : x ≠ y) :
    G.minWeight h ≤ G.L x y :=
  Finset.min'_le _ _ _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨(x, y), Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hxy⟩, rfl⟩)
```
`Finset.min'_le (s) (x) (H2 : x ∈ s) : s.min' _ ≤ x`. Yes.

`minWeight_pos`:
```lean
theorem minWeight_pos (G : FiniteHeatOperator X) (h : ∃ x y : X, x ≠ y) : 0 < G.minWeight h := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hveq⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp (Finset.min'_mem _ _)
  obtain ⟨hp, hpq⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.mp hv
  rw [← hveq]
  exact G.offdiag_pos v.1 v.2 hpq
```
`Finset.min'_mem (s) (H) : s.min' H ∈ s`. Signature: `Finset.min'_mem (s : Finset α) (H : s.Nonempty) : s.min' H ∈ s`. So `Finset.mem_image.mp (Finset.min'_mem _ _)` gives `∃ a ∈ filter, f a = min'`. Then `hp : (v ∈ univ)`, `hpq : v.1 ≠ v.2`. Then rewrite: goal `0 < min'`; `rw [← hveq]` turns goal into `0 < G.L v.1 v.2`; exact offdiag_pos. Good.

Careful: `Finset.min'_mem` might be `Finset.min'_mem : s.min' H ∈ s`. Probe needed.

